    "title": "Why Snorkel AI Simulates Agents Instead of Replaying Traces",
    "source_text": "Snorkel AI pushes \"agent simulations\" over production traces, running millions per month\n\nProduction traces show what an agent did on one run, but they can't be replayed cleanly — database state, tool versions and environments shift, so A/B comparisons never test apples against apples. Snorkel AI's approach converts those traces into offline, repeatable simulation benchmarks that mirror a company's own tools, APIs, policies and workflows, letting agent configurations be compared in parallel on cost, latency and retry counts rather than pass rate alone.",
    "source_path": null,
