            "keyPoints": [
                "Snorkel's pitch: turn production traces into offline simulation environments, then treat those benchmarks as versioned software in CI/CD.",
                "Snorkel says its enterprise environments include thousands of tau-bench-style tasks with databases, policy docs, domain tools and simulated users.",
                "In its insurance underwriting environment, Snorkel reports agent pass@1 rising from 10.9% to 42.0%.",
                "Terminal-Bench 2.1 fixed 28 of the 89 tasks in 2.0 — evidence that even flagship benchmarks rot as dependencies drift.",
                "SnorkelFinance runs agents against 10-K-derived questions with no document access, forcing SQL and code-execution tool use; top models score around 85%.",
                "Gartner expects over 40% of agentic AI projects to be canceled by end-2027, citing costs, unclear value and weak risk controls.",
                "Snorkel's $3M Open Benchmarks Grants pays in compute credits, data access and research collaboration, with results released under open licenses."
            ],
